---
/*
 * Panel6PassThrough - Inflation Section 4.2 element 6, "Pass-through watch."
 *
 * Canon (editorial/dashboard_purpose.md Section 4.2 element 6):
 *
 *   "Side-by-side strip-chart panel:
 *      (USDCAD Y/Y vs goods-ex-energy CPI Y/Y)
 *      (LFS-Micro wage growth vs services-ex-shelter CPI Y/Y).
 *    No regression in basics; the interpretation is analyst prose.
 *    Gated on element 4's derived aggregates landing; if they slip,
 *    pass-through defers to v1.5."
 *
 * Status (2026-05-11): GATED. Four backend derivations are required and
 * none are on disk:
 *   1. processed/usdcad_yoy.csv               - YoY transform on raw FX level.
 *   2. processed/lfs_micro_yoy.csv            - YoY on BoC LFS-Micro wage.
 *      (lfs_wages_all_yoy as a fallback companion is also acceptable.)
 *   3. processed/cpi_goods_ex_energy_yoy.csv  - basket-weighted re-aggregation
 *      of goods CPI excluding the energy sub-index. Per canon 4.2 element 4
 *      the ex-aggregates ship "in v1 only if a reproducible analysis script
 *      with methodology note is in place."
 *   4. processed/cpi_services_ex_shelter_yoy.csv - basket-weighted re-aggregation
 *      of services CPI excluding the shelter sub-index. Same canon gate.
 *
 * Until backend lands all four, this panel renders the canon-compliant
 * "DATA NOT YET WIRED" empty state. The prior implementation passed the
 * raw USDCAD level (CAD/USD) as `primary` to PanelLiveChart with
 * cpi_goods_yoy (%) as `secondary`; the units-mismatch guard then
 * suppressed the secondary and the panel rendered as a USDCAD-level
 * line, which is NOT the pass-through editorial argument. Removed.
 *
 * Backend brief (paste-ready for follow-up dispatch):
 *
 *   Add four derivations to pipeline/build.py (each a wrapper around
 *   transform.timeseries.headline_yoy or a basket-weighted re-aggregator):
 *
 *     - derive_usdcad_yoy           -> processed/usdcad_yoy.csv
 *         Source: raw/usdcad.csv (CAD/USD, daily, FRED DEXCAUS).
 *         Resample to monthly mean before YoY; period_per_year=12.
 *         Methodology note: monthly-mean reflects the pass-through window
 *         that goods CPI samples (CPI is monthly).
 *
 *     - derive_lfs_micro_yoy        -> processed/lfs_micro_yoy.csv
 *         Source: raw/lfs_micro.csv (BoC LFS-Micro composition-adj wage).
 *         Monthly. periods_per_year=12. Companion: lfs_wages_all_yoy
 *         from raw/lfs_wages_all.csv (LFS headline wage) for the optional
 *         secondary line if LFS-Micro stops publishing.
 *
 *     - derive_cpi_goods_ex_energy_yoy   -> processed/cpi_goods_ex_energy_yoy.csv
 *     - derive_cpi_services_ex_shelter_yoy -> processed/cpi_services_ex_shelter_yoy.csv
 *         Both require basket-weighted re-aggregation. Inputs:
 *           - data/derived/cpi_basket_weights_canada_wide.csv (already on disk).
 *           - StatCan Table 18-10-0004-01 component-level monthly indexes
 *             (some on disk via cpi_components.csv; verify component set
 *             matches the canon ex-aggregate definition).
 *         Methodology note required per canon 4.2 element 4. Both YoY,
 *         periods_per_year=12.
 *
 *   Once all four processed CSVs land, this component should be rebuilt
 *   as a bespoke two-pane strip chart (NOT a PanelLiveChart wrapper -
 *   PanelLiveChart is single-panel and cannot host side-by-side strips).
 *   Geometry: 720 x 405 viewBox split into two 350x325 plot areas with a
 *   20px horizontal gutter; each strip carries its own y-axis, shared
 *   x-axis (60-month tail). Canon line/dot/frame/tick treatment per
 *   design/canon_reference_panel.md applies independently to each strip.
 *
 * No synthetic-data fallback. The canon-compliant signal for "this is
 * gated" is the PanelEmpty dashed-border hatch.
 */

import type { PanelData } from "../_shared/panelData";
import PanelEmpty from "../_shared/PanelEmpty.astro";

interface Props {
  data?: PanelData | null;
}

// data prop is accepted for interface uniformity with the SectionLayout
// dispatch table; deliberately unused until backend derivations land.
const { data: _data = null } = Astro.props;
---
<PanelEmpty
  reason="Pass-through derivations gated on basket-weighted CPI ex-aggregates (canon 4.2 element 6)."
  ariaLabel="Pass-through watch: data not yet wired. USDCAD Y/Y, LFS-Micro wage Y/Y, goods-ex-energy CPI Y/Y, and services-ex-shelter CPI Y/Y derivations pending."
/>
